  "keyFindings": [
    "0 of 54 boards (0 of 21 real-lean boards) store a proven ISO tip-off \u2014 every board's tip-off is display-only ('8:30 PM ET'). Therefore capturedAt<tipoff is unprovable and FULLY_RESEARCH_ELIGIBLE = 0.",
    "All 21 real-lean dates are TIMESTAMP_UNPROVEN: they carry market lines (all leans) and strictly-prior trailing features (18 dates fully, 3 partially), blocked ONLY by the missing ISO tip-off.",
    "The 33 empty-scaffold dates are UNUSABLE.",
    "MARKET_ONLY / FEATURES_ONLY / RESULT_ONLY are 0 in this corpus: every real board bundles market+features, and every settled date has a real board.",
    "Capture-time itself is suspect on some dates: boards for 2026-05-18 (gen 20:09 ET) and 2026-06-08 (gen 19:48 ET) were generated same-day-evening ET (near typical tip-off), and 2026-05-18 + 2026-05-19 share the identical generatedAt instant (batch regeneration) \u2014 concrete proof that 'a final board + result exist' does NOT prove a pregame capture.",
    "Settled outcome rows (4,592) exceed pregame board props (2,204): settlement accumulated regenerated/optimizer leans, so most settled rows cannot be tied back to a single proven-pregame board lean."
  ],
  "caveats": [
    "Playoff-only, ~1 month (2026-05-05..2026-06-13), ~16 teams \u2014 not a regular-season claim.",
    "5 real-lean dates (2026-05-05, 2026-05-06, 2026-05-12, 2026-05-13, 2026-06-08) have no settlement \u2014 recoverable only if box scores are re-fetched.",
    "board generatedAt IS an ISO instant (the capture side is provable); the unprovable side is the tip-off. Reconstructing an ISO tip-off (e.g. from the ESPN event feed) is the single change that would move dates from TIMESTAMP_UNPROVEN toward eligibility \u2014 provided every used input is then re-checked pre-tip."
  ],
